@startuml
title One token stream, two candidate readings of `6 * 3 / 2` — declaration order decides

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "**TOKEN STREAM** (identical for both readings)\n`6`   `*`   `3`   `/`   `2`" as TOK #F3F4F6

rectangle "READING A — **ELECTED**" as A #DCFCE7 {
  rectangle "**MulInt** · `*` · <latex>(\ell,r) = (20,21)</latex>" as A_MUL #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**NumLit 6**" as A_6 #E0E7FF
  rectangle "**DivInt** · `/` · <latex>(\ell,r) = (22,23)</latex>" as A_DIV #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**NumLit 3**" as A_3 #E0E7FF
  rectangle "**NumLit 2**" as A_2 #E0E7FF
  rectangle "value <latex>= 6 \times \lfloor 3/2 \rfloor = 6 \times 1 = 6</latex>\nre-printed surface: `6 * 3 / 2` (**unchanged**)" as A_VAL #FEF3C7
}

rectangle "READING B — **NEVER BUILT**" as B #FEE2E2 {
  rectangle "--**DivInt** `/` outermost--" as B_DIV #FCA5A5
  rectangle "--**MulInt** `*` inner--" as B_MUL #FCA5A5
  rectangle "--**NumLit 6**--" as B_6 #FECACA
  rectangle "--**NumLit 3**--" as B_3 #FECACA
  rectangle "--**NumLit 2**--" as B_2 #FECACA
  rectangle "would be <latex>\lfloor (6 \times 3)/2 \rfloor = 9</latex>\nre-printed surface: `(6 * 3) / 2` (**bracketed**)" as B_VAL #FEF3C7
}

TOK -down-> A_MUL : precedence climbing\nabsorbs `*` at floor 0
TOK -down-> B_DIV : the conventional\nleft-to-right reading

A_MUL -down-> A_6 : child 0
A_MUL -down-> A_DIV : child 1, parsed at floor <latex>r = 21</latex>;\n`/` has <latex>\ell = 22 \ge 21</latex>, so it IS absorbed here
A_DIV -down-> A_3
A_DIV -down-> A_2
A_DIV -down-> A_VAL

B_DIV -down-> B_MUL
B_MUL -down-> B_6
B_MUL -down-> B_3
B_DIV -down-> B_2
B_DIV -down-> B_VAL

note right of B_DIV
  To build this, the `*` sub-parse would have
  to STOP before `/`. It cannot: the gate is
  <latex>\ell(\mathtt{/}) \ge \mathrm{floor}</latex>, i.e. <latex>22 \ge 21</latex>, which holds.

  The reading is therefore not merely
  out-ranked in the weight ordering — it never
  enters the shared packed parse forest at all.
end note

note right of A_VAL
  The printer agrees, and that agreement is
  the check. `display.rs` writes reading A as
  `6 * 3 / 2` (no bracket: <latex>\ell(\mathtt{/}) = 22 \ge 21</latex>)
  and reading B as `(6 * 3) / 2`
  (bracket forced: <latex>\ell(*) = 20 < 22</latex>).
  Parser and printer partition the two
  readings by the SAME numbers.
end note

legend bottom
  `*` is declared at `languages/src/calculator.rs:329`, `/` at `:330`.
  `analyze_binding_powers` walks the declaration order and hands out
  <latex>2, 4, 6, \ldots</latex> — so the LATER-declared operator binds TIGHTER.
  Swapping the two source lines swaps the elected reading.
endlegend

@enduml
